  "title": "WBL: Enforcement Perceptions, Parenthood, Public authorities enforce existing legislation on leave benefits for mothers paid by the government",
  "category": "economy",
  "icon": "📊",
  "desc": "The indicator assesses expert perceptions of the extent to which public authorities enforce existing legislation on leave benefits for mothers paid by the government in practice.Experts rate enforcement on a five-point Likert scale (0–4), where 0 indicates no enforcement of protective or beneficial laws, no upholding of women’s rights, or full enforcement of restrictive laws, and 4 indicates full enforcement of protective or beneficial laws, the full upholding of women’s rights, or no enforcement of restrictive laws. Enforcement perceptions indicator-level score is contingent upon the score of the corresponding legal frameworks indicator and calculated by taking the median value of individua",
  "unit": "indicator value",
  "prefix": "",
  "suffix": "",
  "decimals": 1,
  "order": "desc",
